                'title' => 'Règles de contenu',
                'content_markdown' => "# Règles de contenu\n\n### 1. L’esprit de ces règles\n\nBANGO sert à trouver un logement et à faire vivre un quartier. Ces règles existent pour que ces deux choses restent possibles. Elles s'appliquent à tout : publications, reels, stories, commentaires, annonces, messages, pseudonymes et photos de profil.\n\n### 2. Annonces : la vérité d’abord\n\nUne annonce doit correspondre à un bien **réel**, **disponible**, et que vous avez le droit de proposer.\n\nSont interdits :\n\n• l'annonce d'appel — un bien attractif qui n'existe pas, pour attirer des contacts vers un autre ;\n• les photos qui ne sont pas celles du bien, ou qui datent d'un état antérieur sans le dire ;\n• un prix affiché différent du prix réellement demandé, ou des frais non annoncés découverts à la visite ;\n• maintenir en ligne un bien déjà loué. Marquez-le occupé, l'application s'occupe du reste et prévient les personnes qui avaient une visite.\n\n### 3. Argent : ce qui ne se demande jamais\n\nNe demandez jamais, et ne versez jamais, une somme avant une visite. Sont interdits : les « frais de dossier » exigés avant d'avoir vu le bien, les demandes de virement vers un compte personnel, et toute pression à payer vite pour « réserver ».\n\nSignalez immédiatement tout message qui vous demande de l'argent hors des moyens prévus par l'application.\n\n### 4. Discrimination\n\nRefuser un locataire en raison de son origine, de sa nationalité, de son ethnie, de sa religion, de son sexe, de sa situation de famille, de son état de santé ou d'un handicap est interdit, et l'écrire dans une annonce l'est tout autant.\n\nLes critères objectifs liés à la solvabilité et à la capacité à occuper le bien restent légitimes.\n\n### 5. Harcèlement et haine\n\nInterdits : les insultes, les menaces, les contenus qui incitent à la haine ou à la violence contre une personne ou un groupe, la publication d'informations privées sans accord, et la sollicitation répétée d'une personne qui a demandé qu'on cesse.\n\nBloquer n'est pas signaler. Si un comportement est abusif, signalez-le : sans cela, la modération ne le verra pas.\n\n### 6. Contenus sexuels, violents et choquants\n\nLa nudité à caractère sexuel et les contenus pornographiques sont interdits. La violence gratuite, les contenus montrant des blessures graves et les contenus faisant l'apologie du suicide ou des troubles alimentaires le sont également.\n\n### 7. Mineurs\n\nTout contenu mettant en scène des personnes mineures de manière sexualisée est interdit, signalé aux autorités compétentes, et entraîne la fermeture immédiate et définitive du compte. Il n'y a pas de recours.\n\n### 8. Fausses identités\n\nInterdits : se faire passer pour une autre personne, une agence, une administration ou BANGO ; utiliser la photo de quelqu'un d'autre comme photo de profil ; afficher un badge ou un anneau de vérification obtenu par un document falsifié.\n\n### 9. Spam et manipulation\n\nInterdits : les publications répétitives, l'achat ou l'échange d'abonnés, de j'aime ou de commentaires, l'usage de comptes multiples pour gonfler une audience, et les liens trompeurs.\n\n### 10. Illégalités\n\nInterdit, tout contenu qui propose, organise ou facilite une activité illégale : vente de produits réglementés, contrefaçon, jeux d'argent non autorisés, services financiers sans agrément.\n\n### 11. Propriété d’autrui\n\nNe publiez pas de photos, vidéos, musiques ou textes sur lesquels vous n'avez pas de droits. Un titulaire de droits peut nous signaler un contenu ; nous le retirons et prévenons la personne qui l'a publié, laquelle peut contester.\n\n### 12. Mise en avant\n\nUn contenu mis en avant doit respecter toutes les règles ci-dessus, et deux de plus : il ne promet pas un logement qui n'existe pas, et il n'annonce pas un prix qu'il ne tiendra pas.\n\n### 13. Ce qui arrive quand une règle est enfreinte\n\nLa réponse est proportionnée et progressive : avertissement, puis suspension temporaire de la publication, puis fermeture du compte. Les infractions les plus graves — contenus impliquant des mineurs, fraude caractérisée, usurpation — entraînent une fermeture immédiate.\n\nVous êtes toujours informé, avec le motif et le contenu visé, et vous pouvez contester une fois. Un avertissement est retiré de votre dossier après six mois sans nouvel incident.\n\n### 14. Signaler\n\nChaque contenu, chaque profil et chaque conversation porte une option de signalement. Signalez autant de fois que nécessaire : un signalement classé sans suite ne compte jamais contre vous.\n\nSi vous êtes en danger immédiat, contactez d'abord les secours de votre pays. L'application n'est pas un service d'urgence.",
                'effective_date' => '2026-09-01 00:00:00',
                'is_published' => true,
                'published_at' => '2026-09-01 00:00:00',
                'is_mandatory' => false,
            ],
            [
                'slug' => 'terms-of-service',
                'version' => '3.0',
                'locale' => 'en',
                'title' => 'Terms of Use',
                'content_markdown' => "# Terms of Use\n\n### 1. Who publishes BANGO\n\nBANGO is published by CCEDA Finance. The app connects individuals and professionals around neighbourhood content and property listings in several African countries. By creating an account you enter into a contract with CCEDA Finance, governed by these terms and by the law of the country you use the service from.\n\nTogether with the Privacy Policy and the Content Rules, these terms form the entire agreement between you and us. Where the three documents conflict, the Content Rules prevail over these terms on everything concerning what you publish.\n\n### 2. What BANGO is, and what it is not\n\nBANGO is a **host and a technical intermediary**. We provide a publishing space, a messaging service, a listings directory and payment tools. We are not an estate agent, an agent acting on your behalf, or a guarantor.\n\nIn particular:\n\n• we do not visit properties and do not certify that they exist, their condition, or the validity of any title deed;\n• we are not a party to any lease, sale or agreement made between you and another person;\n• we never hold a deposit, a security or rent;\n• a badge, a verification ring or a \"verified\" pill attests to a document check at a point in time. **It is not a guarantee about the property, nor about anyone's solvency or honesty.**\n\nNo money should be paid before visiting the property and seeing an identity document. That advice appears in the app and we ask you to follow it.\n\n### 3. Minimum age and capacity\n\nAccess is reserved for people aged 18 and over. That threshold is not about the content of the platform but about the fact that it allows financial commitments — subscriptions, viewing fees, paid promotion.\n\nWe ask for your date of birth at sign-up. An inaccurate declaration leads to the account being closed without notice and without refund of amounts committed. Where we have serious reason to believe an account belongs to a minor, we suspend it and ask for supporting documents.\n\n### 4. Account, handle and credentials\n\nOne account, one person. Creating several accounts to get around a block, a suspension or a limit is prohibited and leads to all the accounts involved being closed.\n\nThe handle is **unique across the whole platform** and is yours for as long as the account exists. We may reclaim it where it impersonates someone, reproduces a trademark without rights, or is plainly offensive.\n\nYou are responsible for keeping your credentials confidential and for everything done from your account. Turn on the app's biometric lock if your phone is shared. Tell us immediately about any unauthorised access.\n\n### 5. Identity verification and badges\n\nSome functions — publishing a listing, receiving viewing requests, delegating to an agent — require identity verification. You then send us an identity document and, depending on the case, a title deed or a management mandate.\n\nThe badges available are:\n\n• **Landlord badge** — publish and manage properties, receive viewing requests, delegate to agents;\n• **Agent badge** — work on behalf of one or more landlords, run viewings and answer prospects, appear in the agent directory.\n\nA badge is a **subscription**, never a one-off purchase. It runs while it is paid for and while the verification stays current. We may suspend it if a document expires, if a check fails, or in the event of a serious breach of the Content Rules.\n\n### 6. Subscriptions, prices and renewal\n\nBadges are taken monthly or yearly. The price shown before payment is the price due, in your country's currency, excluding any fees charged by your payment operator.\n\n**Renewal.** The subscription renews automatically at the due date unless you turn off auto-renewal from the My subscriptions screen. We tell you before each due date.\n\n**Changing plan.** Moving from monthly to yearly or the other way triggers a pro rata calculation: the unused part of the current period is deducted from the amount due. The breakdown is shown before payment.\n\n**Failed charge.** If a charge fails, the badge stays active during a **seven-day grace period**, during which we retry the payment. After that, with nothing settled, the badge expires.\n\n**Cancellation.** You may cancel at any time. The badge stays active until the end of the period already paid for. **No refund is due for a period started**, except where the law of your country says otherwise.\n\n### 7. What happens when a badge expires\n\nNothing is deleted. That is a commitment on our part, and the platform keeps it:\n\n• your listings are **unpublished**, not erased. They leave search and the property feed, and come back exactly as they were — photos, texts, statistics, conversations — as soon as you reactivate;\n• the access you had granted to agents goes **dormant**. Those agents are notified, their ongoing conversations become read-only and come back to you;\n• any running promotion campaign stops, and the unspent budget comes back as BANGO credit;\n• your account, posts, reels, followers, messaging and payment history are untouched.\n\n### 8. Promoting content\n\nPromotion applies to **published content** — a post or a reel — and never to a property listing. That rule is not technical: a listing is judged on its characteristics, and paying to jump the queue would distort a housing search.\n\nPromoted content is marked **Sponsored**.\n\nThe budget is committed when payment is approved and spent as delivery runs. If the campaign stops before the end — by your choice, by a moderation decision, or because the content was deleted — the unspent part comes back as **BANGO credit**.\n\nWe may refuse or interrupt a promotion whose content breaches the Content Rules, without that giving rise to anything beyond the return of the unspent budget.\n\n### 9. BANGO credit\n\nBANGO credit is an internal unit of account, usable to pay for a badge, a promotion or viewing fees.\n\n• It **cannot be bought**. It comes only from an unspent campaign budget, a settled double charge, or a goodwill gesture on our part.\n• It **cannot be withdrawn** in Mobile Money, converted to cash, or transferred to another account.\n• It does not expire while the account exists. **It disappears with the account**: use it before deleting.\n\n### 10. Payments and Mobile Money\n\nPayments go through Mobile Money operators and, in some countries, bank cards. We are not the payment institution: the transaction is carried out by the operator, under its own terms.\n\n**Your PIN never passes through the app.** You enter it on your phone, in your operator's interface. No BANGO screen will ever ask for it; if that happens, it is an attempted fraud and we ask you to report it.\n\nIf you are charged twice, report it from the app with the transaction reference and your operator's SMS. After checking with them, the extra amount is credited back as BANGO credit within 72 hours.\n\nIf the network drops during an approval, **do not retry the payment**: you would risk a double charge. The app queries the operator and tells you as soon as the status is known.\n\n### 11. Viewing fees\n\nSome viewings are paid. The amount, who receives it and the cancellation terms are shown before any payment.\n\nA viewing fee pays for the organisation and travel of the person who receives you. **It is not a reservation of the property, a deposit, or a guarantee of tenancy.**\n\nCancellation: refunds follow the terms shown at booking time. If the landlord or agent cancels, or if the property turns out to be unavailable, the fee is refunded in full.\n\n### 12. Delegating to an agent\n\nA landlord may authorise an agent to act on their properties. Authorisation is given **capability by capability**: run viewings, answer messages, publish, edit a listing.\n\nTwo things are never delegated: **changing a price** and **taking payment**.\n\nEvery action by an agent is logged under their name. The landlord can withdraw access at any time; the agent is told, their conversations become read-only and return to the landlord. A revoked agent is never erased: their history stays readable, because it may serve as proof of a past exchange.\n\n### 13. Your content and the rights you grant us\n\nYou remain the **owner** of everything you publish. You grant us a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free licence to host, reproduce, technically adapt and display that content, **solely in order to run the service**.\n\nThat licence:\n\n• lasts while the content is published and ends when it is deleted, subject to backups and legal retention obligations;\n• does not allow us to sell your content, or to use it in advertising outside the platform without your express agreement;\n• does not extend to content you share in private messages, except to deliver and store it for you.\n\nYou warrant that you hold the rights to what you publish, in particular to property photos and to the image of the people who appear in them.\n\n### 14. Shared links and deleted content\n\nContent shared outside the app leaves links that outlive its deletion. When you delete content, we offer to redirect those links to your page or to another listing, or to leave them showing an explicit page. That redirect is reversible at any time.\n\n### 15. What is prohibited\n\nThe Content Rules set out what can be published. The following are also prohibited and may lead to immediate closure of the account:\n\n• publishing a listing for a property that does not exist, is not available, or that you neither own nor hold a mandate for;\n• asking for payment before any viewing, or outside the means provided by the app;\n• impersonating a person, an agency or BANGO;\n• bulk-extracting platform data by any means;\n• circumventing a technical measure, testing the security of the service without written authorisation, or exploiting a flaw instead of reporting it;\n• creating an account to get around a block or a sanction.\n\n### 16. Moderation, sanctions and appeals\n\nWe may remove content, restrict a function, suspend or close an account in the event of a breach. The measure is proportionate: a first warning restricts nothing, a second decision suspends posting, a third closes the account.\n\n**You are told** about any decision concerning you, with its reason and the content involved.\n\n**You may challenge** each decision, once, from the app. The appeal is reviewed by someone who did not take the original decision. If the appeal succeeds, the content is restored and the effects of the measure are lifted.\n\nA report that leads to no action never counts against the person who filed it.\n\n### 17. Service availability\n\nWe do our best to keep the service running, without committing to a figure. Interruptions may happen for maintenance, updates, or because of a third party — network operator, hosting provider, payment operator.\n\nWe may change the app's functions. If a change removes a function you pay for, you may cancel and get a refund of the unused part of your subscription.\n\n### 18. Liability\n\nWe are liable for direct damage caused by a breach of these terms on our part.\n\nWe are not liable for:\n\n• content published by users, which we did not author;\n• agreements made between users, or their performance;\n• the condition, compliance or availability of a property;\n• money paid outside the app;\n• a failure of your payment operator or your network.\n\nNothing in these terms limits our liability for gross negligence, wilful misconduct, or personal injury.\n\n### 19. Deleting your account\n\nYou can delete your account from the app. Deletion becomes **final after thirty days**; during that window, simply signing in cancels it and restores everything.\n\nBefore you confirm, the app tells you precisely what deletion changes **for other people**: listings withdrawn, agents losing authorisation, campaigns stopped, conversations turned read-only.\n\nSome data survives deletion where the law requires it: accounting records and payment evidence, material needed to defend a legal claim, and material tied to an ongoing moderation decision.\n\nIf you only want to stop renting out, the app offers to **unpublish your listings** without closing the account.\n\n### 20. Changes to these terms\n\nWe may change these terms. Any substantial change is notified in the app **thirty days** before it takes effect, with a summary of what changed.\n\nIf you do not accept the new version, you may cancel your subscriptions and delete your account before it takes effect; the unused part of your subscriptions is then refunded.\n\nThe version in force and the date you accepted are always available on this screen.\n\n### 21. Governing law and disputes\n\nThese terms are governed by the law of the country you use the service from, where that law contains mandatory consumer-protection provisions. Failing that, Senegalese law applies.\n\nBefore any action, please write to us from the Help Centre: the vast majority of disagreements are settled there. You keep in any event the right to bring proceedings where you live and, where applicable, to refer the matter to a consumer mediation body.\n\n### 22. Contacting us\n\nSupport and complaints: in the app, Profile → Support. A ticket is opened there and tracked, with a reference.\n\nSecurity vulnerability reports: securite@bango.app. We undertake not to pursue any good-faith report that causes neither damage nor disclosure.\n\nPost: CCEDA Finance — BANGO legal department.",
                'effective_date' => '2026-09-01 00:00:00',
                'is_published' => true,
                'published_at' => '2026-09-01 00:00:00',
