            [
                'slug' => 'content-rules',
                'version' => '3.0',
                'locale' => 'en',
                'title' => 'Content rules',
                'content_markdown' => "# Content rules\n\n### 1. The spirit of these rules\n\nBANGO is for finding a home and keeping a neighbourhood alive. These rules exist so that both stay possible. They apply to everything: posts, reels, stories, comments, listings, messages, handles and profile photos.\n\n### 2. Listings: truth first\n\nA listing must match a **real** property, **available**, and one you have the right to offer.\n\nProhibited:\n\n• the bait listing — an attractive property that does not exist, used to pull contacts towards another;\n• photos that are not of the property, or that show an earlier state without saying so;\n• a price shown that differs from the price actually asked, or undisclosed fees discovered at the viewing;\n• keeping an already-let property online. Mark it taken; the app does the rest and warns the people who had a viewing booked.\n\n### 3. Money: what is never asked for\n\nNever ask for, and never pay, money before a viewing. Prohibited: \"file fees\" demanded before seeing the property, requests to transfer to a personal account, and any pressure to pay quickly to \"reserve\".\n\nReport immediately any message asking you for money outside the means provided by the app.\n\n### 4. Discrimination\n\nRefusing a tenant because of their origin, nationality, ethnicity, religion, sex, family situation, health or a disability is prohibited, and writing it in a listing equally so.\n\nObjective criteria about solvency and ability to occupy the property remain legitimate.\n\n### 5. Harassment and hate\n\nProhibited: insults, threats, content inciting hatred or violence against a person or a group, publishing private information without agreement, and repeatedly contacting someone who has asked you to stop.\n\nBlocking is not reporting. If behaviour is abusive, report it: otherwise moderation will not see it.\n\n### 6. Sexual, violent and shocking content\n\nSexual nudity and pornographic content are prohibited. So are gratuitous violence, content showing serious injuries, and content glorifying suicide or eating disorders.\n\n### 7. Minors\n\nAny content sexualising minors is prohibited, reported to the competent authorities, and leads to immediate and permanent closure of the account. There is no appeal.\n\n### 8. False identities\n\nProhibited: passing yourself off as another person, an agency, an administration or BANGO; using someone else's photo as your profile picture; displaying a badge or verification ring obtained with a forged document.\n\n### 9. Spam and manipulation\n\nProhibited: repetitive posting, buying or trading followers, likes or comments, using multiple accounts to inflate an audience, and misleading links.\n\n### 10. Illegal activity\n\nProhibited: any content offering, organising or facilitating illegal activity — sale of regulated goods, counterfeiting, unlicensed gambling, unauthorised financial services.\n\n### 11. Other people’s property\n\nDo not publish photos, videos, music or texts you have no rights to. A rights holder can report content to us; we remove it and tell the person who published it, who can challenge.\n\n### 12. Promotion\n\nPromoted content must respect all the rules above, and two more: it does not promise a home that does not exist, and it does not advertise a price it will not honour.\n\n### 13. What happens when a rule is broken\n\nThe response is proportionate and progressive: a warning, then a temporary posting suspension, then closure of the account. The most serious breaches — content involving minors, established fraud, impersonation — lead to immediate closure.\n\nYou are always told, with the reason and the content involved, and you may challenge once. A warning is removed from your file after six months without a further incident.\n\n### 14. Reporting\n\nEvery piece of content, every profile and every conversation carries a report option. Report as often as needed: a report that leads to no action never counts against you.\n\nIf you are in immediate danger, contact your country's emergency services first. The app is not an emergency service.",
